{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And Isaac pleaded.</b> Rashi explained: much, and he persisted in prayer. And I say: every occurrence of the root עתר has the sense of persistence and multiplication. And if you ask: what does this teach us? Rashi explained to say: and I say, every occurrence of עתר has the sense of persistence and multiplication. Rather, one may answer: at first Rashi explained what he received from his teachers — that specifically ויעתר is the language of persistence and multiplication, and afterward he explained his own view — that even every occurrence of עתר is the language of persistence and multiplication." "<b>Opposite his wife.</b> For the rectification of his wife, like נכח ה׳ דרככם, whose Aramaic translation is אתקן ארחתהון. But on his own behalf he would not have prayed, for he knew that he was not sterile, as it is written: כי ביצחק יקרא לך זרע." "<b>For she was barren.</b> Why was Rebekah barren? So that the nations would not say: our prayer that we prayed over our sister — 'may you become thousands of myriads' — produced the fruit. Rather, ויעתר יצחק, and ויעתר לו."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "The comment quotes Rashi twice in close succession; the repetition is in the source text and has been preserved."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:05:52.719273365Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}